 # Design decision log
 
 *Scratch space: decisions recorded and not yet carried through, trimmed once applied on main. Written only through
-`just decisions`. Next: 1*
+`just decisions`. Next: 6*
+
+### 1 A refused entry says why on stderr
+
+**Context.** When `add` refuses an entry (an empty account, a zero amount), does it print the reason alone or the reason and the usage text? Options: (1) the reason alone, one line (2) the reason, then the usage text. The run picked (1) and acted on it; the independent agent of `/answer-doubt` picked (2): the two answers disagree (no owner ruling).
+**Decision.** A refused entry prints its reason alone, one line on stderr, and exits 1; the usage text is for a missing argument.
+**Automated.** disagreed
+**Affected.** [Entries](rules/ledger.md#Entries)
+**Source.** [Q1](reviews/2026-11-24-void-entry-1.md#Q1%20A%20refused%20entry%20says%20why%20on%20stderr)
+**Status.** recorded 2026-11-24
+
+### 2 The balance of an unknown account is 0.00
+
+**Context.** What does `balance` print for an account that has no entry? Options: (1) `0.00` (2) an error, no such account. The run picked (1) and acted on it; the independent agent of `/answer-doubt` picked (2): the two answers disagree (no owner ruling).
+**Decision.** `tally balance` of an account without entries prints `0.00`, as the rule that such an account has balance 0 says.
+**Automated.** disagreed
+**Affected.** [Balances](rules/ledger.md#Balances)
+**Source.** [Q2](reviews/2026-11-24-void-entry-1.md#Q2%20The%20balance%20of%20an%20unknown%20account%20is%200.00)
+**Status.** recorded 2026-11-24
+
+### 3 Account names are compared as typed
+
+**Context.** Are `Acme` and `acme` one account or two? Options: (1) two accounts, names compared as typed (2) one account, names compared without case. The run picked (1) and acted on it; the independent agent of `/answer-doubt` picked (2): the two answers disagree (no owner ruling).
+**Decision.** Account names are compared exactly as typed: `Acme` and `acme` are two accounts.
+**Automated.** disagreed
+**Affected.** [Entries](rules/ledger.md#Entries)
+**Source.** [Q3](reviews/2026-11-24-void-entry-1.md#Q3%20Account%20names%20are%20compared%20as%20typed)
+**Status.** recorded 2026-11-24
+
+### 4 The report lists an account whose balance is zero
+
+**Context.** Does the report list an account whose entries add up to zero? Options: (1) yes, one row per account that has entries (2) no, only accounts with a balance. The run picked (1) and acted on it; the independent agent of `/answer-doubt` picked (2): the two answers disagree (no owner ruling).
+**Decision.** The report lists every account that has entries, a zero balance included.
+**Automated.** disagreed
+**Affected.** [Rows](rules/reports.md#Rows)
+**Source.** [Q4](reviews/2026-11-24-void-entry-1.md#Q4%20The%20report%20lists%20an%20account%20whose%20balance%20is%20zero)
