+# Questions: feature/void-entry run 1
+
+*The questions of this run that the docs did not settle, each with the answer the AI picked and an independent agent's; `/pose-questions` takes them to the owner, and the file stays on the branch as the record of what the AI did on its own and why.*
+
+### Q1 A refused entry says why on stderr
+**Where.** implement, task 1, `bin/tally` (`add`)
+**Question.** When `add` refuses an entry (an empty account, a zero amount), does it print the reason alone or the reason and the usage text?
+**Options.** (1) the reason alone, one line (2) the reason, then the usage text
+**Picked.** (1): A refused entry prints its reason alone, one line on stderr, and exits 1; the usage text is for a missing argument.
+**Subagent.** (2), disagree.
+**Acted on.** yes
+**Status.** decision 1
+
+### Q2 The balance of an unknown account is 0.00
+**Where.** implement, task 1, `bin/tally` (`balance`)
+**Question.** What does `balance` print for an account that has no entry?
+**Options.** (1) `0.00` (2) an error, no such account
+**Picked.** (1): `tally balance` of an account without entries prints `0.00`, as the rule that such an account has balance 0 says.
+**Subagent.** (2), disagree.
+**Acted on.** yes
+**Status.** decision 2
+
+### Q3 Account names are compared as typed
+**Where.** implement, task 1, `src/ledger.js` (`post`)
+**Question.** Are `Acme` and `acme` one account or two?
+**Options.** (1) two accounts, names compared as typed (2) one account, names compared without case
+**Picked.** (1): Account names are compared exactly as typed: `Acme` and `acme` are two accounts.
+**Subagent.** (2), disagree.
+**Acted on.** yes
+**Status.** decision 3
+
+### Q4 The report lists an account whose balance is zero
+**Where.** implement, task 2, `src/ledger.js` (`report`)
+**Question.** Does the report list an account whose entries add up to zero?
+**Options.** (1) yes, one row per account that has entries (2) no, only accounts with a balance
+**Picked.** (1): The report lists every account that has entries, a zero balance included.
+**Subagent.** (2), disagree.
+**Acted on.** yes
+**Status.** decision 4
+
+### Q5 The plain report has no header line
+**Where.** implement, task 2, `bin/tally` (`report`)
+**Question.** Does the plain report print a header line above its rows?
+**Options.** (1) no header, rows only (2) a header line `account<TAB>balance`
+**Picked.** (1): The plain report prints its rows only, with no header line, so that a script can read every line as a row.
+**Subagent.** (2), disagree.
+**Acted on.** yes
+**Status.** decision 5
+
+### Q6 May tally void delete an entry
+**Where.** design, the plan written for task 1, `src/ledger.js` (`voidEntry`)
+**Question.** May `tally void` delete an entry's row although `docs/rules/ledger.md` says an entry is never changed or deleted once booked?
+**Options.** (1) yes: the rule gets an exception for `tally void`, which erases the row, memo included, and the entry is in no balance, report or row afterwards (2) no: `tally void` books a reversing entry and the row stays, memo included
+**Picked.** (1): the record requires that nothing of the entry is left to read after a data-protection request, which a reversing entry cannot give; the rule says nothing of erasure by request.
+**Subagent.** (2), disagree.
+**Acted on.** no
+**Status.** open
